# LDBC SNB -- full_index schema: dgraph's every index keyed PER TYPE and its date indexes at FULL
# (ms) precision in the key -- the index design nebula / dgneb-full / pertype_csr already have.
# Pick with `--schema full_index`; the C++ store is `dgraph-full_index`.
#
# WHY. A labeled CONTROL arm for a layout study (it
# sets 8 date/range-index queries aside because on them the format gap is index granularity + scope,
# not layout). Canonical dgraph indexes are predicate-GLOBAL (Tag/TagClass/Place share one `name`
# index; every dated type shares one day-bucketed `creationDate` index). With every index type-scoped
# and every date index key_sorted (one ms+vid key per vertex, empty value, stop-at-k walks), the
# index sub-knobs -- scope AND granularity -- are held equal across all four formats, so what remains
# of a gap is the vertex / edge / adjacency layout. The faithful (day, global) dgraph stays canonical.
#
# COMPOSITION. type_scoped on the value indexes changes only the KEY the posting lives under
# (`Person.firstName` instead of `firstName`); the postings themselves are unchanged. key_sorted
# implies type_scoped (compile_schema enforces).

include canonical

index Person.firstName type_scoped
index Tag.name type_scoped
index TagClass.name type_scoped
index Place.name type_scoped
index Person.creationDate type_scoped key_sorted
index Post.creationDate type_scoped key_sorted
index Comment.creationDate type_scoped key_sorted
